# rust.config - safe configuration fragment for Rust on 4.19
#
# This fragment is applied on top of the main defconfig:
#   scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh -m -O out out/.config rust.config
#   make O=out ARCH=arm64 LLVM=1 CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- olddefconfig
#
# The options below are not compatible with rustc on 4.19. The CFI in
# this tree is the classic LTO-based CFI, not KCFI.
#
# Note: in the whyred-perf baseline the options below were already off.
# This fragment still exists so the disabling is explicit and does not
# rely on defconfig defaults.
# POLLY_CLANG is deliberately left on here: the baseline has it enabled,
# and turning it off would add an unrelated change.
# KSU and NoMount are deliberately not in here: they come from the base
# config, not from this fragment.
# NOTE: do not write symbol names in the comments in this header,
# because merge_config.sh can misread a comment as a config line.
# CONFIG_MODVERSIONS is not set
# CONFIG_CFI_CLANG is not set
# CONFIG_SHADOW_CALL_STACK is not set
# CONFIG_LTO_CLANG is not set
# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF is not set
# CONFIG_TRIM_UNUSED_KSYMS is not set
# CONFIG_KASAN is not set
# CONFIG_FUNCTION_TRACER is not set
